Keep readable fallback polling active without spinning on writable sockets.

Solaris can lose a later readable event-port edge after an fd is re-associated,
so moving a drained readable direction entirely back to the event port can hang
Tokio. Keep registered interests in the bounded fallback poll, but remove a
continuously writable direction from its event-port association until poll(2)
observes that it has drained. This preserves readable and EOF liveness while
preventing POLLOUT from making port_getn return continuously.

